// Math is rendered as MathML, which browsers lay out themselves.

--- equation-inline ---
The value $x$ is small.
│ <p>The value <math><mi>x</mi></math> is small.</p>

--- equation-block ---
$ x + y = z $
│ <math display="block"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></math>

--- fraction ---
$ x/2 $
│ <math display="block"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>

--- attachments ---
$ a_1^2 $
│ <math display="block"><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></math>

--- root ---
$ sqrt(x) $
│ <math display="block"><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></math>

--- root-with-index ---
$ root(3, x) $
│ <math display="block"><mroot><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mroot></math>

--- primes ---
$ f'(x) $
│ <math display="block"><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>

--- operator ---
$ sin(x) $
│ <math display="block"><mrow><mo lspace="0.1667em" rspace="0.1667em">sin</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>

--- operator-with-limits ---
$ lim_(n -> oo) a_n $
│ <math display="block"><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1667em" rspace="0.1667em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>→</mo><mo>∞</mo></mrow></munder><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></math>

--- delimited ---
$ (a + b) $
│ <math display="block"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></math>

--- vector ---
$ vec(a, b) $
│ <math display="block"><mrow><mo stretchy="true">(</mo><mtable columnalign="center"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo stretchy="true">)</mo></mrow></math>

--- cases ---
$ cases(a, b) $
│ <math display="block"><mrow><mo stretchy="true">{</mo><mtable columnalign="left"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></math>

--- matrix ---
$ mat(a, b; c, d) $
│ <math display="block"><mrow><mo stretchy="true">(</mo><mtable columnalign="center"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>d</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo stretchy="true">)</mo></mrow></math>

--- aligned-rows ---
$ x &= y \
  z &= w $
│ <math display="block"><mtable columnalign="right left"><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>z</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></math>

--- rows-without-alignment ---
$ x = y \
  z = w $
│ <math display="block"><mtable columnalign="center"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></math>

--- accent ---
$ hat(x) $
│ <math display="block"><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>̂</mo></mover></math>

--- underline ---
$ underline(x) $
│ <math display="block"><munder accentunder="true"><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="true">̲</mo></munder></math>

--- cancel ---
$ cancel(x) $
│ <math display="block"><mrow style="text-decoration:line-through"><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>

--- styled-text ---
$ bold(x) + sans(y) $
│ <math display="block"><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝘺</mi></mrow></math>

--- numbers-and-names ---
$ 12 + x + "text" $
│ <math display="block"><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>text</mi></mrow></math>

--- labelled-equation ---
$ x = y $ <eq>
│ <math display="block" id="eq"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></math>

--- delimited-around-a-fraction ---
// Delimiters grow only around content that is taller than a line of symbols.
// A fraction is; see delimited, where `(a + b)` is not.
$ (x/2) $
│ <math display="block"><mrow><mo stretchy="true">(</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="true">)</mo></mrow></math>

--- delimited-around-a-superscript ---
// A script is barely taller than the letter it sits on, and a delimiter that
// grew for it would be visibly too big.
$ (v^beta) $
│ <math display="block"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></math>

--- delimited-nested-around-a-fraction ---
// The inner group has the fraction, so both grow.
$ ((x/2)) $
│ <math display="block"><mrow><mo stretchy="true">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="true">(</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="true">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">)</mo></mrow></math>

--- delimited-with-a-mid ---
// A mid follows the group it sits in.
$ { x mid(|) x > 0 } $
│ <math display="block"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></math>

--- delimited-with-a-mid-around-a-fraction ---
$ { x mid(|) x > 1/2 } $
│ <math display="block"><mrow><mo stretchy="true">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="true">}</mo></mrow></math>
